{"title":"Potential energy","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Potential_Energy\">Potential Energy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Potential_energy&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Potential Energy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Potential energy is quite literally the amount of energy an object has relative to its potential. The most common type of potential energy is gravitational potential energy, or U, given by the formula mass*gravity*height of dropping point. Other notable theorems including the Conservation of energy theorem, Ki+Ui=Kf+Uf.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018103443\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.003 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.004 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 2/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27486:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018103443 and revision id 218319. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}